{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none. The program is prior-only with respect to data: no top-level data variable appears on the left side of a sampling statement. The declared `cases` data are not scored by the model.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The model uses only built-in sampling statements for top-level parameters, each parameter has exactly one prior, and there is no protected observed likelihood to rewrite.
","model_safe_stan":"functions {
  array[] real sir(real t, array[] real y, array[] real theta,
                   array[] real x_r, array[] int x_i) {
    real S = y[1];
    real I = y[2];
    real R = y[3];
    real N = x_i[1];

    real beta = theta[1];
    real gamma = theta[2];

    real dS_dt = -beta * I * S / N;
    real dI_dt = beta * I * S / N - gamma * I;
    real dR_dt = gamma * I;

    return {dS_dt, dI_dt, dR_dt};
  }
}
data {
  int<lower=1> n_days;
  array[3] real y0;
  real t0;
  array[n_days] real ts;
  int N;
  array[n_days] int cases;
}
transformed data {
  array[0] real x_r;
  array[1] int x_i;
  x_i[1] = N;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> gamma;
  real<lower=0> beta;
  real<lower=0> phi_inv;
}
transformed parameters {
  array[n_days, 3] real y;
  real phi = 1. / phi_inv;
  {
    array[2] real theta;
    theta[1] = beta;
    theta[2] = gamma;

    y = integrate_ode_rk45(sir, y0, t0, ts, theta, x_r, x_i);
  }
}
model {
  beta ~ normal(2, 1);
  gamma ~ normal(0.4, 0.5);

  //col(matrix x, int n) - The n-th column of matrix x
  phi_inv ~ exponential(5);
}
generated quantities {
  real R0 = beta / gamma;
  real recovery_time = 1 / gamma;
  array[n_days] real pred_cases;
  pred_cases = neg_binomial_2_rng(col(to_matrix(y), 2) + 1e-5, phi);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N": 5, "cases": [2, 3], "n_days": 2, "t0": 0.0, "ts": [1.0, 2.0], "y0": [6.720025627408752, 2.9645613069034793, 4.592388911870451]}","protected_variables":[]}
